course: dictionary
lesson: 14767
title: Prostrate: flat, low and overcome
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a body is placed. Prostrate means lying flat on the ground with your face down. Read the clues around it: «The knight lay prostrate in the mud after his fall.» He is in the mud, flat, after a fall, so prostrate must mean lying flat.
explain: Prostrate can also be a verb. To prostrate yourself means to lie face down, often to pray or to show great respect. «The crowd prostrated themselves before the king.» People bow low and lie flat to honour him, so the clue is respect.
explain: Prostrate can also mean completely weak or overcome. «She was prostrate with grief when the news came.» Grief is a deep sadness, so the words after prostrate tell you how she felt. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Prostrate means lying flat on the ground with your face down.
fact: «He lay prostrate on the floor.» Here the word describes the position of a body.
fact: To prostrate yourself means to lie face down, often to worship, pray or show great respect.
fact: In prayer, some people prostrate themselves: Muslims do this in sujood, and Bible stories tell of people bowing down before God or kings.
fact: «Prostrate with grief» or «prostrate with heat» means completely overcome or worn out.
exercise: «The tired hiker lay prostrate on the grass.» What does prostrate describe? | Running very fast | Standing tall with arms raised | Sitting on a chair | *Lying flat with the face down
exercise: Ayesha reads, «The worshippers prostrated themselves in prayer.» What does prostrated mean? | Ate a large meal | *Lay face down to pray or show respect | Jumped up and cheered | Walked away quietly
exercise: «The villagers were prostrate with heat after the long summer day.» What does prostrate suggest? | Cold and wet | Full of energy and ready to dance | *Completely worn out and weak | Hungry for dinner
test: «After the bad news, he was ___ with grief.» Which word fits the gap? | Curious | *Prostrate | Noisy | Cheerful
test: Why might someone prostrate themselves in a religious place? | To sleep in a comfy bed | To count their coins | *To show great respect or to pray | To win a race
exam: Which word means the same as overcome in «prostrate with grief»? | *Overwhelmed | Joyful | Loud | Curious
